---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ProseShell from "../components/ProseShell.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const updated = new Date().toLocaleDateString("en-US", {
	year: "numeric",
	month: "long",
	day: "numeric",
});
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy | MS/MBA: Engineering Sciences"
	description="What the waitlist form collects, where it is stored, and how to have your details removed."
	bodyClass="bg-paper"
>
	<ProseShell eyebrow="Privacy" title="What this site collects">
		<p>
			Short version: an email address if you choose to give one, plus which version of the page you
			were reading. Nothing else, and nothing is sold or shared.
		</p>

		<h2>If you submit the form</h2>
		<p>When you enter your email address, four things are recorded:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>The email address you typed.</li>
			<li>Which of the three page versions you submitted from.</li>
			<li>
				Whether you asked to join the waitlist or to request an information session.
			</li>
			<li>
				Any campaign parameters in the link you arrived through, which indicate where the link was
				shared rather than anything about you.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			This is stored in Cloudflare Workers KV, on infrastructure operated by Cloudflare. It is used
			to follow up with program details and to understand which description of the program people
			respond to. If an email service is connected, your address is also passed to it for the
			purpose of sending you that follow-up.
		</p>

		<h2>Analytics</h2>
		<p>
			This site uses <a href="https://plausible.io/">Plausible</a>, which is privacy-first and
			cookie-free. It does not collect personal data, does not track you across sites, and does not
			build a profile of you. It records aggregate counts: page views, which version was viewed, and
			whether a visitor submitted the form or opened a question.
		</p>
		<p>
			The video on the parent page is embedded through YouTube's no-cookie domain, so YouTube does
			not set a tracking cookie unless you press play.
		</p>

		<h2>What does not happen</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Your details are never sold, rented, or shared with third parties for their own use.</li>
			<li>There is no advertising network on this site and no advertising cookie.</li>
			<li>You are not tracked across other websites.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Removing your details</h2>
		<p>
			You can ask to have your email address deleted at any time, and it will be removed from
			storage and from any connected email service. Send the request from the address you signed up
			with, to the same contact you received program follow-up from, and say you would like your
			details deleted.
		</p>

		<h2>This is an independent site</h2>
		<p>
			This site is run by a student in the program, not by Harvard. It is not an official Harvard
			publication, and submitting the form here is not an application to any Harvard program. See <a
				href="/about">About this site</a
			> for more.
		</p>

		<p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {updated}</p>
	</ProseShell>
	<Footer />
</Layout>
